/* -- The portrait, inlined ---------------------------------------------
   The halftone reads the picture back out of a canvas pixel by pixel, and a
   canvas is tainted the moment an image from another origin is drawn into it.
   On file:// every file IS another origin, so loading portrait.webp from disk
   poisons the read and getImageData throws SecurityError -- the marks vanish
   and only the caption is left. A data: URI is never treated as cross-origin,
   so the same bytes arriving this way keep the canvas clean and the page works
   opened straight off the disk as well as served.

   Generated from portrait.webp; regenerate this file rather than editing it.
   The .webp is still on disk and is still the source of truth. */
window.PORTRAIT_SRC = 'data:image/webp;base64,';
